      "heading": "A projectile motion application",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "A ball is thrown upward with initial velocity 15 m/s from a height of 2 m, so its acceleration is $a(t)=-9.8$ m/s$^2$. Find its velocity function $v(t)$ and position function $s(t)$.",
          "answer": "$v(t)=\\int a(t)\\,dt=-9.8t+C_1$. Using $v(0)=15$: $v(t)=-9.8t+15$. $s(t)=\\int v(t)\\,dt=-4.9t^2+15t+C_2$. Using $s(0)=2$: $s(t)=-4.9t^2+15t+2$."
        }
      ]
